IMPORT policy

§ `Query facts — the nine benchmark questions`

-- Standing preamble applied to every question (per inputs/queries-blind.md):
-- assume every condition and exclusion unrelated to the question is
-- satisfied / not triggered, and that the agreement is signed and the
-- premium paid on time (policy.l4 does not model those two facts at all, so
-- there is nothing to set for them here).
--
-- Shared defaults used below whenever a fact is not mentioned by a question
-- (chosen so they never themselves trigger an exclusion or a cancelation):
--   * `month of hospitalization`  = 0   (well inside both the 7- and 12-month
--                                        marks, unless the question fixes it)
--   * `age at hospitalization`    = 30  (well under the 80-year exclusion)
--   * every `caused by ...` flag  = FALSE
--   * both wellness-visit fields  = NOTHING (still pending; not yet due,
--                                        since the default hospitalization
--                                        month of 0 is under 7)
--   * fraud/misrepresentation/withholding = FALSE

§§ `Q1 — firefighter duty burns`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while doing
--  my duty as a firefighter?"
-- The burns are explicitly incurred while doing firefighter duty, so this
-- arises directly out of "service as a fire fighter" — General Exclusion
-- §2.1 item 3 is triggered. Everything else is unrelated to this question
-- and is set to the non-triggering default.

q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 0
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 30
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS TRUE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS NOTHING
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS NOTHING
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q1

§§ `Q2 — 78 years old at hospitalization`

-- "will my policy apply if I am 78 years old at the time of hospitalization?"
-- 78 is below the "equal to or greater than 80" threshold of §2.1 item 5, so
-- the age exclusion does not trigger. No cause of hospitalization is given,
-- so no other exclusion is in play either.

q2 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 0
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 78
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS NOTHING
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS NOTHING
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q2

§§ `Q3 — pneumonia, 5 months in, age 65`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for pneumonia 5 months after
--  the policy's effective date, and my age at the time of hospitalization is
--  65?"
-- Pneumonia is a sickness, not one of the excluded activities; age 65 is
-- under 80; 5 months is comfortably inside both the 7-month and 12-month
-- marks, so §1.3 is still pending and the policy has not expired.

q3 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 5
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 65
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS NOTHING
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS NOTHING
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q3

§§ `Q4 — fall abroad, wellness confirmation at 8 months`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to a fall while traveling
--  abroad and I had given confirmation of my wellness visit 8 months after
--  the policy's effective date?"
-- Being abroad does not exclude coverage (§3.1: worldwide, 24/7); a fall is
-- not one of the excluded activities. But confirmation at month 8 is later
-- than the 7-month deadline of §1.3, so that condition was not satisfied in
-- a timely fashion and the policy was canceled under §1.2 — regardless of
-- when the underlying visit itself took place, which this question does not
-- say, so it is set (month 6) to a value that would itself have been timely,
-- isolating the late confirmation as the only operative fact.

q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 0
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 30
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS JUST 6
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS JUST 8
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q4

§§ `Q5 — self-inflicted prank injury, no fraud`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for punching my own face to
--  show off for my friends and I did not commit fraud or misrepresentation?"
-- Punching one's own face to show off is not any of the five listed
-- exclusions (skydiving / military / firefighter / police / age >= 80) —
-- the policy text names no "intentional act" or "self-inflicted injury"
-- exclusion at all, so none is invented here. Fraud/misrepresentation is
-- expressly negated by the question, so §1.2's cancelation-for-fraud ground
-- is not triggered either.

q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 0
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 30
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS NOTHING
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS NOTHING
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q5

§§ `Q6 — skydiving injury, age 79, wellness confirmation at 6.5 months`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to an injury sustained
--  while skydiving, my age at the time of hospitalization was 79, and proof
--  of my wellness visit was provided 6.5 months after the policy's
--  effective date?"
-- Skydiving alone trips General Exclusion §2.1 item 1, regardless of age
-- (79 is under 80 and so does not independently exclude) or of the
-- wellness-visit timing (6.5 <= 7, and the visit itself is set to month 6,
-- <= 6, so §1.3 is satisfied on these facts) — the skydiving exclusion is
-- outcome-determinative on its own.

q6 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 0
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 79
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS TRUE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS JUST 6
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS JUST 6.5
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q6

§§ `Q7 — heart attack, wellness confirmation at 2 months, age 75`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for a heart attack, proof of
--  the wellness visit was submitted 2 months after the policy's effective
--  date, and my age at the time of hospitalization was 75?"
-- A heart attack is not an excluded activity; age 75 is under 80;
-- confirmation (and the visit itself) at month 2 is well inside both the
-- 6- and 7-month marks, so §1.3 is satisfied.

q7 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 0
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 75
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS JUST 2
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS JUST 2
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q7

§§ `Q8 — military training injury, within term, no fraud`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized after being injured in a
--  military training exercise, the hospitalization occurred within the
--  policy term, and I did not commit fraud?"
-- Being injured in a military training exercise arises directly out of
-- "service in the military" — General Exclusion §2.1 item 2 is triggered.
-- "Within the policy term" is given concretely as month 3 (any value under
-- 12 represents it); absence of fraud is expressly stated.

q8 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 3
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 30
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS TRUE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS NOTHING
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS NOTHING
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q8

§§ `Q9 — son bit claimant's ankle, wellness confirmation at 6 months, police officer`

-- "will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to my son biting me in the
--  ankle, proof of my wellness visit was provided 6 months after the
--  effective date, and I was serving as a police officer at the time of
--  hospitalization?"
-- Being a police officer "at the time of hospitalization" is a status, not a
-- cause: the ankle bite is a domestic incident that does not arise directly
-- or indirectly out of "service in the police" (contrast Q1 and Q8, where
-- the injury is explicitly incurred while performing the service's duties).
-- So `caused by police service` is FALSE here — the exclusion is not about
-- the claimant's occupation, only about what the hospitalizing event arose
-- out of. Confirmation (and the visit itself) at month 6 satisfies §1.3
-- ("no later than" the 6th/7th month, i.e. AT MOST, so exactly 6 qualifies).

q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `month of hospitalization`                            IS 0
    `age at hospitalization`                               IS 30
    `caused by skydiving`                                  IS FALSE
    `caused by military service`                           IS FALSE
    `caused by firefighter service`                        IS FALSE
    `caused by police service`                             IS FALSE
    `month of the wellness visit`                          IS JUST 6
    `month the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`   IS JUST 6
    `guilty of fraud, misrepresentation, or withholding`   IS FALSE

#EVAL `covered` q9
